WEBVTT

00:00:01.030 --> 00:00:05.900
A Notice from the Yamayuri Council
When watching
"Maria Watches Over Us ~Printemps~,"
please have the room brightly lit and
sit well away from the television set.

00:00:07.170 --> 00:00:09.930
At the beginning of March, shortly
before the graduation ceremony...

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:12.670
...where we would say goodbye to the
Lady Roses who had looked after us,

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:15.930
Tsutako-san came to me with a terrible dilemma.

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:18.580
What are these?

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:20.070
Photographic evidence.

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:25.680
Rosa Foetida has been on multiple dates,
each time with a different man?!

00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:27.360
The men she's been seen with...

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:31.420
...range from men in their 20s to
their 50s and vary in terms of type,

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:33.400
but the one thing they have in common...

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:35.960
...is that they're all rich, adult men.

00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:39.670
Furthermore, Rosa Foetida
has not been going home lately,

00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:41.570
but instead, staying at luxury hotels.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.630
Hotels? Why?

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:46.310
It just goes to show that when you
take the easy route to get things,

00:00:46.310 --> 00:00:48.500
you still pay a certain price for it.

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:50.700
Price? What do you mean?

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:54.080
At any rate, I'll leave the rest to you.

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:55.950
What? Leave the rest of what to me?

00:00:56.480 --> 00:00:58.450
I'm going to leave these photos in your keeping.

00:00:58.690 --> 00:01:00.850
What?! Why me?!

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:03.460
If it's too burdensome for you,

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:05.980
tear them up and throw them
away with your trash at home.

00:01:06.490 --> 00:01:07.620
Good day.

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:10.020
Wait a minute! Tsutako-san!

00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:18.100
Just what do you expect me
to do with these photos?

00:01:33.190 --> 00:01:34.050
All right!

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:36.090
Eri-chan.

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:38.850
Thank you for the clothes. Do they suit me?

00:01:39.490 --> 00:01:41.860
You look cute. Like a little bunny rabbit.

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:43.360
Shall we go?

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:52.470
The maidens, who flock to
Maria-sama's garden,

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:57.340
pass through the tall gates today yet
again with innocent, angelic smiles.

00:01:58.010 --> 00:02:02.210
Their pure hearts and bodies are
clad in deep-colored uniforms.

00:02:02.650 --> 00:02:05.490
So that the pleats of their
skirts are not disturbed...

00:02:05.490 --> 00:02:08.580
...and so that their white sailor
collars are not set aflutter,

00:02:08.690 --> 00:02:11.850
it is customary here to walk
slowly and with decorum.

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:17.590
The Private Lillian Girls' Academy,
a garden of maidens.

00:02:26.670 --> 00:02:30.610
Maria Watches Over Us
Printemps

00:02:32.250 --> 00:02:39.590
In the morning mist,
Asamoya no naka

00:02:39.650 --> 00:02:46.460
the white path goes on.
tsuzuku shiroi michi

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:53.960
The birds sing.
Tori no saezuri

00:02:54.670 --> 00:03:01.600
We exchange greetings.
Aisatsu kawashinagara

00:03:02.210 --> 00:03:09.210
At times, the clouds hang low,
Toki ni kumo ga tarekomete

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:16.520
and the sun may grow dim.
hizashi kagerou tomo

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:24.620
But I will walk with my chin up,
Sesuji nobashite aruku

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:32.140
for I know,
watashi wa shitteru kara

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:39.150
that above those heavy clouds...
omoi kumo no ue wa

00:03:39.150 --> 00:03:47.080
...is the blue sky.
aoi sora

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:53.930
The Yellow Rose at Full Tilt

00:04:02.870 --> 00:04:05.240
I'll give the photos to Rosa Foetida.

00:04:05.370 --> 00:04:07.310
That's probably the best thing to do.

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:09.640
Good morning, Yumi-chan.

00:04:12.650 --> 00:04:13.810
It's been a while.

00:04:15.620 --> 00:04:17.810
Rosa Foetida, good morning.

00:04:18.650 --> 00:04:19.640
Her scarf!

00:04:19.750 --> 00:04:23.290
Rosa Foetida is known for having
the Academy's most neatly tied scarf,

00:04:23.290 --> 00:04:24.690
and yet, it's crooked!

00:04:26.230 --> 00:04:27.330
Oh, this?

00:04:27.330 --> 00:04:29.900
I sent it out to be dry cleaned
at a different place than usual...

00:04:29.900 --> 00:04:32.200
...and they put a crease in it at a weird spot.

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:35.160
I shifted the knot to hide it.

00:04:37.440 --> 00:04:41.100
Um, where did you come
from today, Rosa Foetida?

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:44.410
Where? From my home, as usual.

00:04:46.580 --> 00:04:49.050
The Rosa Foetida really is staying at hotels...

00:04:49.380 --> 00:04:50.580
Well, see you later.

00:04:54.390 --> 00:04:57.450
I missed my chance to give her the photos...

00:05:00.030 --> 00:05:03.230
So basically, Girl A is not
even going back home...

00:05:03.230 --> 00:05:05.830
...and spending nights out on the
town with different men every night.

00:05:05.830 --> 00:05:07.470
That's what it comes down to, right?

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:09.730
And she's always in the company of rich men.

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:12.870
Yes, hypothetically speaking,
that's what it comes down to.

00:05:12.870 --> 00:05:14.480
Hypothetically this, hypothetically that.

00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:17.000
Your story has been censored way too much.

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:19.480
I need you to give me the
story concisely from the start.

00:05:20.010 --> 00:05:23.470
But I can't very well tell her
this is about Rosa Foetida...

00:05:24.350 --> 00:05:27.880
To put it bluntly, Girl A is
going on subsidized dates.

00:05:28.460 --> 00:05:30.450
She might also have run away from home.

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:34.220
Those are just objective generalizations
based on your info, though.

00:05:35.330 --> 00:05:37.090
Subsidized... dates...

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:39.760
The price that Tsutako-san was talking about...

00:05:40.470 --> 00:05:42.130
Just leave her alone.

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:44.140
She's probably doing it because she wants to.

00:05:44.340 --> 00:05:46.770
She's the only one who's going
to get hurt and have regrets.

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:50.380
But the person in question is Rosa Foetida...

00:05:50.380 --> 00:05:52.510
...and I can't exactly leave this matter alone...

00:05:55.750 --> 00:05:57.480
So, you see, Yoshino-san...

00:05:58.120 --> 00:05:59.920
It's still cold outside.

00:06:01.120 --> 00:06:03.760
A teacher detained us concerning
committee business,

00:06:03.760 --> 00:06:05.020
so that made us late.

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:06.320
I'll make tea.

00:06:13.370 --> 00:06:15.840
My Onee-sama is thoroughly fastidious,

00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:18.600
not to mention, she dislikes men,
so I can't go to her for advice.

00:06:19.010 --> 00:06:21.070
If there's anyone I can talk to...

00:06:21.340 --> 00:06:22.400
No, not her.

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:24.680
Rei-sama is a straightforward sort of person,

00:06:24.680 --> 00:06:27.710
so I feel like she might directly
confront Rosa Foetida.

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:32.910
I can't talk to Yoshino-san, either.

00:06:32.990 --> 00:06:35.320
Once she gets an idea in her head,
she tends to rush headlong with it,

00:06:35.320 --> 00:06:37.850
so in a sense, she might be
even more dangerous than Rei-sama.

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:39.680
Shimako-san is...

00:06:39.990 --> 00:06:42.800
...dependable, but she's
still something of a mystery,

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:45.200
so I don't know if I can go
to her for this sort of thing.

00:06:47.900 --> 00:06:49.240
Yumi, are you listening?

00:06:49.240 --> 00:06:49.930
Y-Yes!

00:06:50.670 --> 00:06:51.870
What are you doing?

00:06:52.110 --> 00:06:54.810
We are talking about the send-off
ceremony for the third-year students.

00:06:54.810 --> 00:06:55.870
Pay attention.

00:06:56.110 --> 00:06:57.540
Pardon me.

00:07:01.050 --> 00:07:04.420
I wonder if it might just be
best to talk to Rosa Chinensis.

00:07:04.420 --> 00:07:05.550
Hey, there!

00:07:07.590 --> 00:07:09.110
Rosa Gigantea!

00:07:09.620 --> 00:07:12.590
Yumi-chan, you've been wanting
to see me, haven't you?

00:07:12.660 --> 00:07:14.320
Is this what you wanted me to do?

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:16.490
N-No.

00:07:16.900 --> 00:07:18.760
That's strange.

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:21.930
I got this feeling that you were calling for me.

00:07:22.070 --> 00:07:23.900
Then, was it you who called me?

00:07:25.840 --> 00:07:26.900
Lunch!

00:07:27.070 --> 00:07:30.130
Lunch? This is Goronta.

00:07:30.580 --> 00:07:33.880
Among the first-year students,
we call him Lunch.

00:07:34.850 --> 00:07:36.540
Do you want to try some too, Yumi-chan?

00:07:36.650 --> 00:07:38.310
Dry cat food.

00:07:38.550 --> 00:07:40.580
No, thank you.

00:07:46.030 --> 00:07:47.460
Rosa Gigantea...

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:48.590
What?

00:07:48.700 --> 00:07:52.890
Remember how you once said that
Rosa Foetida suffers hardship?

00:07:53.170 --> 00:07:55.500
Did I ever say such a thing?

00:07:55.900 --> 00:07:59.770
That she's too good at everything
and the outcome is predictable,

00:07:59.770 --> 00:08:03.230
and that's why she always
looks bored and unmotivated.

00:08:03.540 --> 00:08:07.650
I did say that, but that's not a painful hardship.

00:08:07.650 --> 00:08:09.910
It's a luxurious sort of hardship, if you will.

00:08:10.180 --> 00:08:13.720
Eriko's the type who's always
seeking out and living for...

00:08:13.720 --> 00:08:16.380
...stimulating experiences that will surprise her.

00:08:17.330 --> 00:08:18.790
Stimulating experiences...

00:08:19.460 --> 00:08:21.190
Is something up with Eriko?

00:08:21.930 --> 00:08:24.690
Now would be my chance to tell her,
but what should I do?

00:08:25.870 --> 00:08:28.430
I guess I'm going to be saying
goodbye to this place soon.

00:08:29.270 --> 00:08:30.700
A lot of things happened,

00:08:30.840 --> 00:08:35.500
but because I had Yoko and Eriko,
life here wasn't all that bad.

00:08:38.850 --> 00:08:41.370
I'll refrain from talking to any third-year students.

00:08:41.850 --> 00:08:42.950
It's right before graduation.

00:08:42.950 --> 00:08:45.350
I don't want to tarnish their
memories of their friends.

00:08:57.300 --> 00:08:58.560
Rosa Foetida.

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:02.990
Yumi-chan.

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:05.570
What are you doing?

00:09:06.110 --> 00:09:07.070
Nothing...

00:09:07.910 --> 00:09:10.140
I'm troubled, because I can do nothing.

00:09:10.680 --> 00:09:14.940
What is this sense of ennui
I feel coming from her?

00:09:15.680 --> 00:09:18.950
If you are feeling ill, perhaps you
should go to the nurse's office.

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:23.080
No, it's not that there's anything
physically wrong with me.

00:09:23.360 --> 00:09:25.190
I'm sorry to have worried you.

00:09:25.590 --> 00:09:27.030
I'll go back to the classroom.

00:09:27.960 --> 00:09:29.260
That's the wrong way!

00:09:37.410 --> 00:09:38.600
Rosa Foetida...

00:09:41.840 --> 00:09:43.500
When you think about it,

00:09:44.180 --> 00:09:47.150
it's not as if college is your
only choice after graduation.

00:09:47.850 --> 00:09:51.680
If you don't go to college, will you find a job?

00:09:53.450 --> 00:09:56.390
Oh, I forgot you could do that, too.

00:09:57.160 --> 00:09:59.890
Other than college and finding a job, that leaves...

00:10:02.360 --> 00:10:03.850
I want to get married...

00:10:06.270 --> 00:10:07.000
What?!

00:10:08.070 --> 00:10:11.630
Oh, I want to be the wife of
an umbrella-making ronin!

00:10:12.040 --> 00:10:13.670
An umbrella-making ronin?

00:10:14.210 --> 00:10:15.980
The poor samurai in historical dramas,

00:10:15.980 --> 00:10:21.040
who makes umbrellas on
the side to make a living?

00:10:23.850 --> 00:10:25.080
Wouldn't that be fantastic?

00:10:25.420 --> 00:10:28.550
Why the wife of an umbrella-making ronin?

00:10:30.220 --> 00:10:32.920
I'm apparently a hypsilophodon!

00:10:33.430 --> 00:10:34.160
Huh?

00:10:36.300 --> 00:10:37.530
It's a dinosaur.

00:10:37.730 --> 00:10:41.000
Yumi-chan, have you ever been
compared to a dinosaur?

00:10:42.300 --> 00:10:43.840
It was a first for me, too.

00:10:43.840 --> 00:10:45.500
That's why it gave me the chills!

00:10:49.010 --> 00:10:50.440
Rosa Foetida...

00:10:50.850 --> 00:10:52.210
Has she completely lost it?!

00:10:55.050 --> 00:10:56.850
Rosa Foetida is getting married?!

00:10:57.220 --> 00:10:58.780
This is a scoop!

00:11:07.700 --> 00:11:08.490
Hypsilophodon Family

00:11:08.760 --> 00:11:12.530
How could a dinosaur and the wife of
an umbrella-making ronin be related?

00:11:14.170 --> 00:11:16.690
A new man in Rosa Foetida's life.

00:11:16.970 --> 00:11:20.530
Tsutako-san, let's stop doing this already.

00:11:24.250 --> 00:11:25.540
Rosa Chinensis!

00:11:28.220 --> 00:11:30.220
Since you called this one "new,"

00:11:30.220 --> 00:11:33.910
it sounds as though there
are other men in Eriko's life.

00:11:38.630 --> 00:11:43.060
The one man that stands out from the
rest is definitely most intriguing.

00:11:43.430 --> 00:11:46.760
Rosa Foetida accepted a roasted
sweet potato from this man.

00:11:46.870 --> 00:11:47.930
A roasted sweet potato?

00:11:48.400 --> 00:11:50.600
In front of the elephant exhibit at the zoo.

00:11:50.770 --> 00:11:53.970
After that, Rosa Foetida
went and bought canned coffee.

00:11:54.480 --> 00:11:58.710
Rather than a date, it seemed like they
were just watching the elephants.

00:11:59.010 --> 00:12:01.570
Eriko has a soft spot for oddballs, after all.

00:12:01.880 --> 00:12:03.610
Soft spot for oddballs?

00:12:04.550 --> 00:12:07.350
Two years ago, the person Eriko
chose to be her little sister...

00:12:07.350 --> 00:12:10.620
...was a girl who was tall and lanky like a boy.

00:12:10.690 --> 00:12:11.660
Rei-sama...

00:12:11.930 --> 00:12:16.330
Eriko has a soft spot for types
that she's never been around.

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:17.400
I see.

00:12:17.970 --> 00:12:21.800
You see, if her degree of
interest is below a certain level,

00:12:21.800 --> 00:12:24.370
Eriko can make pretty levelheaded decisions,

00:12:24.370 --> 00:12:27.710
but once it surpasses that level,
she no longer sees anything else,

00:12:27.710 --> 00:12:28.770
so it becomes troublesome.

00:12:29.210 --> 00:12:32.200
Eriko's illness may be serious this time.

00:12:32.480 --> 00:12:37.080
But Rosa Foetida said there was
nothing physically wrong with her.

00:12:39.250 --> 00:12:40.520
I'm talking about being lovesick.

00:12:41.990 --> 00:12:43.760
Several days later,

00:12:43.760 --> 00:12:46.890
Rosa Foetida's love developed
in an unexpected direction...

00:12:47.660 --> 00:12:50.860
...because of the article
published by the Lillian Ledger.

00:12:52.770 --> 00:12:54.230
What is this?!

00:12:55.140 --> 00:12:57.100
Rei-chan, calm down.

00:12:58.340 --> 00:13:00.140
I can't be calm about this!

00:13:00.240 --> 00:13:01.440
This makes it sound...

00:13:01.440 --> 00:13:04.970
...as if my Onee-sama is dating
a different man every night!

00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:10.580
It's rather entertaining as
a piece of fiction, though.

00:13:10.650 --> 00:13:14.020
The heroine, Yellow Rose, begins working
part-time at an escort service...

00:13:14.960 --> 00:13:17.790
...and after being with all sorts of rich men,

00:13:17.790 --> 00:13:20.730
she's rebuked by a male teacher from
her school and comes to her senses.

00:13:20.800 --> 00:13:24.430
In time, she begins to have romantic
feelings for that teacher.

00:13:24.430 --> 00:13:26.420
Please stop, Rosa Gigantea!

00:13:26.970 --> 00:13:28.370
Don't worry, Rei.

00:13:28.770 --> 00:13:31.600
Most of this is speculation
made in the guise of fiction.

00:13:31.940 --> 00:13:35.880
What do you mean by "most of this," Onee-sama?

00:13:36.640 --> 00:13:39.770
Yumi-chan, show those photos to everyone.

00:13:39.850 --> 00:13:40.870
Oh, all right.

00:13:44.950 --> 00:13:45.940
Huh?

00:13:46.550 --> 00:13:47.610
These people are...

00:13:48.090 --> 00:13:49.610
It's so like Eriko, right?

00:13:50.460 --> 00:13:51.290
Seriously.

00:13:52.830 --> 00:13:54.850
What are these photos?!

00:13:55.500 --> 00:13:57.930
Please explain it to us, Onee-sama.

00:14:00.070 --> 00:14:02.800
Year 3, Chrysanthemum Class, Torii Eriko-san,

00:14:02.800 --> 00:14:05.290
please come to the Non-Curricular
Guidance Office immediately.

00:14:08.110 --> 00:14:09.540
Non-Curricular Guidance Office

00:14:11.510 --> 00:14:14.240
My! What is this commotion about, ladies?

00:14:14.920 --> 00:14:18.680
We have come to speak to you
regarding Torii Eriko-san.

00:14:23.660 --> 00:14:25.490
This is quite a crowd!

00:14:31.230 --> 00:14:34.200
All the men in the photographs are here!

00:14:39.570 --> 00:14:41.040
Rosa Foetida...

00:14:44.610 --> 00:14:47.410
So everyone involved got summoned?

00:14:47.750 --> 00:14:48.940
That's not it.

00:14:49.220 --> 00:14:53.220
These four charged into the faculty
office and made a big fuss,

00:14:53.220 --> 00:14:54.650
and that was why I was summoned.

00:14:55.390 --> 00:14:57.560
To think they would take
a school paper seriously...

00:14:57.560 --> 00:14:59.860
...and go to the trouble of meeting
with the Academy Director...

00:14:59.860 --> 00:15:01.090
They're crazy.

00:15:02.400 --> 00:15:05.330
As if we could remain silent after
a story like this was printed!

00:15:05.530 --> 00:15:07.730
You are ever the worrywart...

00:15:08.900 --> 00:15:10.200
...aren't you, sir?

00:15:10.670 --> 00:15:12.570
Oh, Yoko-chan and Sei-kun...

00:15:13.370 --> 00:15:15.870
And you guys were worried
about your sister, too?

00:15:16.680 --> 00:15:16.940
Yes.

00:15:16.940 --> 00:15:17.640
Yes.
Yes.

00:15:18.080 --> 00:15:18.740
What?!

00:15:19.210 --> 00:15:20.980
Then these people are...

00:15:21.550 --> 00:15:23.780
My father and my elder brothers.

00:15:24.250 --> 00:15:28.480
Then, you were going on dates every
night with members of your family?

00:15:28.790 --> 00:15:31.850
Yes. I had declined to while I was
studying for my college exams,

00:15:32.330 --> 00:15:34.190
but once my acceptance was announced,

00:15:34.190 --> 00:15:38.390
all the men in my family were
vying to monopolize my time,

00:15:38.570 --> 00:15:40.190
so I haven't even had time to go home.

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:42.940
The men of the Torii family...

00:15:42.940 --> 00:15:46.240
...have always utterly adored
Eriko, who is the youngest.

00:15:46.470 --> 00:15:49.480
To think my fanatical brothers and doting father...

00:15:49.480 --> 00:15:51.810
...compete with each other
to go on dates with me...

00:15:51.910 --> 00:15:53.740
It's beyond embarrassing.

00:15:55.780 --> 00:15:57.380
By the way, Director,

00:15:57.750 --> 00:16:00.880
it says here that Eriko is romantically
involved with an Academy teacher.

00:16:01.120 --> 00:16:04.060
Is this school paper article true?

00:16:04.890 --> 00:16:05.720
It is not.

00:16:06.930 --> 00:16:08.490
That was fiction.

00:16:09.260 --> 00:16:11.870
Because I was unable to
corroborate the rumors...

00:16:11.870 --> 00:16:15.300
...that Rosa Foetida was going
on dates with various men.

00:16:15.470 --> 00:16:17.940
And yet, you wanted to make
an article of it, didn't you?

00:16:18.140 --> 00:16:21.010
And an article that would kindle
people's interest, to boot.

00:16:21.780 --> 00:16:24.800
Then, nothing written here is true?

00:16:24.910 --> 00:16:27.570
There's no teacher that you're in love with, right?

00:16:29.250 --> 00:16:29.980
There is...

00:16:30.520 --> 00:16:31.750
...someone I love, at least.

00:16:31.990 --> 00:16:32.820
What?!
What?!

00:16:35.220 --> 00:16:38.420
Who the hell is it that duped Eri-chan?!

00:16:38.960 --> 00:16:41.050
I haven't been duped.

00:16:41.460 --> 00:16:43.190
Where is this man?!

00:16:44.300 --> 00:16:45.290
The zoo.

00:16:46.570 --> 00:16:49.230
It's someone who works at the zoo?

00:16:49.470 --> 00:16:53.510
No. He goes to see the elephants
when he has time off work.

00:16:53.510 --> 00:16:56.480
Because he likes to look at large animals.

00:16:57.180 --> 00:17:01.410
And this person's occupation
is probably fixing umbrellas.

00:17:06.420 --> 00:17:07.790
The umbrella-making ronin!

00:17:16.130 --> 00:17:17.190
Why...

00:17:18.500 --> 00:17:19.730
That is because...

00:17:20.100 --> 00:17:24.870
...I saw 4 of the 5 men you've
been with arrive at the school,

00:17:24.940 --> 00:17:27.370
and I thought it would be a pity if
the last man were to be left out.

00:17:27.840 --> 00:17:28.900
Tsutako-san!

00:17:29.240 --> 00:17:32.770
I thought I might run into him if I went
to the zoo, and what do you know?

00:17:32.950 --> 00:17:35.610
May I ask what your name is?

00:17:36.250 --> 00:17:38.340
Uh, pardon my late introduction.

00:17:39.250 --> 00:17:43.690
I teach science at the neighboring
Hanadera Academy's high school.

00:17:43.690 --> 00:17:44.950
My name is Yamanobe.

00:17:45.530 --> 00:17:46.190
Why...

00:17:46.190 --> 00:17:48.720
Why you! How dare you do this to our Eriko!

00:17:48.830 --> 00:17:50.520
If you behave rudely towards him,

00:17:51.100 --> 00:17:52.690
I will not forgive you.

00:17:55.270 --> 00:17:59.870
Um, why exactly was I summoned here?

00:18:00.870 --> 00:18:01.840
Yamanobe-san,

00:18:03.410 --> 00:18:04.500
please...

00:18:05.280 --> 00:18:06.510
...marry me.

00:18:11.390 --> 00:18:13.720
T-This is Lillian's
Non-Curricular Guidance Office!

00:18:13.720 --> 00:18:16.660
To think a student would
propose marriage to a man!

00:18:16.660 --> 00:18:17.850
This is unprecedented.

00:18:25.600 --> 00:18:26.930
Which would you bet on?

00:18:27.400 --> 00:18:29.430
It probably won't be much of a bet.

00:18:33.370 --> 00:18:34.970
I refuse.

00:18:36.740 --> 00:18:37.770
Why?!

00:18:39.180 --> 00:18:41.150
Is it because of our 10-year age difference?

00:18:41.580 --> 00:18:43.750
Is it because you spend all the
money you earn as a teacher...

00:18:43.750 --> 00:18:47.740
...on dinosaur fossil digs
and you have no savings?

00:18:48.420 --> 00:18:52.360
So that's what the dinosaur-loving
umbrella-making ronin was about.

00:18:53.130 --> 00:18:55.250
Those are all valid,

00:18:55.630 --> 00:19:00.260
but the greatest reason is that I do not love you.

00:19:00.530 --> 00:19:02.800
No, let me put that differently.

00:19:03.800 --> 00:19:07.300
Not once have I considered you to
be a possible romantic interest.

00:19:07.570 --> 00:19:08.940
I mean, what do you expect?

00:19:09.310 --> 00:19:11.910
Since we first met by accident at the zoo,

00:19:11.910 --> 00:19:14.610
we have still only seen each other
three times, including today.

00:19:15.720 --> 00:19:18.690
Even in terms of total hours,
it can't be more than 3 hours.

00:19:18.920 --> 00:19:19.940
Excuse me.

00:19:21.320 --> 00:19:23.550
We have spent at least three
and a half hours together.

00:19:25.190 --> 00:19:26.860
Though, it might have seemed short to you,

00:19:26.860 --> 00:19:30.300
because you spent a lot of time
looking at the elephants.

00:19:32.130 --> 00:19:34.430
Do you have the day off today?

00:19:35.070 --> 00:19:37.440
Yes, on days when I don't have class,

00:19:37.440 --> 00:19:40.100
I sometimes come to the zoo like this.

00:19:40.640 --> 00:19:42.130
To see the elephants?

00:19:42.880 --> 00:19:44.100
Why do you ask?

00:19:44.650 --> 00:19:46.240
Because you were watching them so intently.

00:19:48.550 --> 00:19:49.280
Yes.

00:19:49.780 --> 00:19:51.580
I like large animals.

00:19:51.750 --> 00:19:52.680
Large?

00:19:53.520 --> 00:19:55.080
Then, like whales, too?

00:19:56.060 --> 00:19:58.420
The truth is, I want to see dinosaurs.

00:20:00.560 --> 00:20:02.360
Looking at elephants, I imagine...

00:20:02.360 --> 00:20:07.460
...that stegosauruses were probably
about the same size, for example.

00:20:07.570 --> 00:20:08.660
What about me?

00:20:08.940 --> 00:20:09.730
What?

00:20:11.770 --> 00:20:15.000
Does any dinosaur come to
mind when you look at me?

00:20:15.780 --> 00:20:16.970
Let me think...

00:20:17.240 --> 00:20:19.010
A hypsilophodon, maybe.

00:20:19.080 --> 00:20:21.980
A stegoceras might be a little too big, I think.

00:20:24.890 --> 00:20:26.010
I understand.

00:20:26.590 --> 00:20:29.650
I'm glad. So you understand.

00:20:30.320 --> 00:20:32.220
But I am not satisfied.

00:20:32.530 --> 00:20:33.060
What?

00:20:33.060 --> 00:20:35.760
I wanted to know more about you,

00:20:35.760 --> 00:20:38.000
so I was continually asking
you all sorts of questions,

00:20:38.000 --> 00:20:41.260
but I realize now that I was being too unilateral.

00:20:41.670 --> 00:20:45.800
From now on, please come to know me,
even if it's just little by little.

00:20:46.110 --> 00:20:48.440
You will come to know more about me...

00:20:48.440 --> 00:20:50.770
...and I will come to know even more about you.

00:20:51.210 --> 00:20:53.710
And having done that,
if we come to love one another,

00:20:53.710 --> 00:20:55.810
please marry me then.

00:20:56.150 --> 00:20:57.310
That would be fine, then.

00:20:57.920 --> 00:20:59.480
I am in agreement.

00:21:00.090 --> 00:21:02.780
That would not be fine! I do not approve!

00:21:03.090 --> 00:21:05.690
If you object too much,

00:21:05.690 --> 00:21:09.820
you will eventually have a daughter
who keeps her relationships a secret.

00:21:10.860 --> 00:21:12.260
That would be bad...

00:21:12.570 --> 00:21:16.430
Yamanobe-sensei is certain to
conduct a restrained courtship.

00:21:18.140 --> 00:21:22.130
Yamanobe-sensei, I think
you had better agree to this.

00:21:22.380 --> 00:21:25.280
She's the type of girl who will
only chase you if you run,

00:21:25.680 --> 00:21:28.550
and her nickname is "Snapping Turtle Eriko."

00:21:32.320 --> 00:21:34.050
A-All right.

00:21:34.450 --> 00:21:36.510
If you would be fine with just being friends.

00:21:43.530 --> 00:21:45.900
The school paper is apparently
publishing an extra edition...

00:21:45.900 --> 00:21:48.460
...to apologize for the "Yellow Rose"
commotion and revise the story.

00:21:48.540 --> 00:21:49.870
That sounds fine.

00:21:50.140 --> 00:21:50.760
Oh.

00:21:52.010 --> 00:21:52.940
Goronta.

00:21:53.210 --> 00:21:55.670
So you call him Goronta, too.

00:21:56.110 --> 00:21:58.010
But that's what Sei calls him.

00:22:00.010 --> 00:22:01.610
Come here, Goronta.

00:22:06.790 --> 00:22:09.720
He must have found something nice.

00:22:10.320 --> 00:22:12.590
Whenever she finds something
that catches her fancy,

00:22:12.590 --> 00:22:15.080
Rosa Foetida runs headlong after it,

00:22:15.460 --> 00:22:18.120
and I thought that made
her a little like the cat.

00:23:27.730 --> 00:23:29.100
Bonjour, Yoshino.

00:23:29.170 --> 00:23:30.470
Hello, Yoshino.

00:23:30.640 --> 00:23:31.730
Bonjour, Yumi.

00:23:31.810 --> 00:23:33.100
Hello, Yumi.

00:23:33.370 --> 00:23:34.670
Comment allez-vous?

00:23:34.740 --> 00:23:36.210
How are you?

00:23:36.280 --> 00:23:37.870
Je vais bien, merci.

00:23:37.980 --> 00:23:39.500
I am well, thank you.

00:23:39.610 --> 00:23:40.480
Au revoir.

00:23:40.780 --> 00:23:41.610
Good-bye.

00:23:41.820 --> 00:23:45.680
At Lillian, both "bonjour" and
"au revoir" are " gokigenyou."

00:23:46.090 --> 00:23:46.620
Next time on "Maria Watches Over Us,"

00:23:46.620 --> 00:23:48.220
Next time on "Maria Watches Over Us,"
Next Time "Most Dreadfully Busy Days"

00:23:48.220 --> 00:23:48.620
Next Time "Most Dreadfully Busy Days"

00:23:48.620 --> 00:23:50.020
"Most Dreadfully Busy Days."
Next Time "Most Dreadfully Busy Days"

00:23:50.020 --> 00:23:50.360
Next Time "Most Dreadfully Busy Days"

00:23:50.360 --> 00:23:54.390
In old Japanese, the "most" would be
translated as "extremely" or " utterly."
Next Time "Most Dreadfully Busy Days"

00:23:54.390 --> 00:23:56.190
